<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/043Y">Definition <span data-tag="043Y">8.2.1.1</span>.</a> Let $\lambda : \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}^{\operatorname{op}} \times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$ be a coupling of $\infty $-categories and let $C$ be an object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, having image $\lambda (C) = (C_{-}, C_{+} ) \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}^{\operatorname{op}} \times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$. We say that $X$ is <em>universal</em> if it is an initial object of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times _{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+} } \{ C_{+} \} $, and <em>couniversal</em> if it is an initial object of the $\infty $-category $\{  C_{-} \}  \times _{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}^{\operatorname{op}} } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. </p>
